# 1. Mission, product scope and engineering objective

HOMIO / REOS is intended to become a unified, global, AI-enabled real-estate operating system supporting international brokerage, broker SaaS, builder SaaS, enterprise operations and partner integrations.

The backend must provide one coherent, secure and recoverable business platform—not a collection of disconnected APIs, agents, databases and microservices.

Its core business lifecycle is:

**Identity → Tenant → Builder/Project → Inventory Acquisition → Verification → Publication → Search → Customer Enquiry → Lead Qualification → Ownership → Communication → Site Visit → Offer → Deal → Trust/Fraud Governance → Commission → Settlement → Reconciliation → Reporting.**

The platform must support AI-assisted and policy-governed automation across this lifecycle without creating parallel business engines.

## 1.1 Backend-only scope

This master controls:

- Public backend API and private runtime integration.
- API contracts, authentication, authorization and tenant enforcement.
- Domain adapters and business workflow orchestration.
- Persistence, transaction integrity and data ownership.
- Search, retrieval, AI integration and safe autonomous execution.
- Events, durable workflows, background processing and recovery.
- Security, privacy, compliance and external integrations.
- Backend testing, CI, deployment and production operations.

Explicitly excluded:

- Frontend pages and layouts.
- UI components and visual interactions.
- CSS, themes, design tokens and animations.
- Responsive presentation and visual UX.
- Frontend-only implementation and styling.

Backend-to-frontend API contracts remain in scope. The frontend consumes backend-owned contracts and must not become a second business or authorization engine.

## 1.2 Supported business modes

The unified backend must support these operating modes through configuration, tenant policy and entitlement boundaries:

1. Owned international brokerage.
2. Broker SaaS.
3. Builder SaaS.
4. Enterprise and white-label.
5. Platform and API partners.

These modes must not become five independent backend systems.

Pune is the initial market focus. The domain model must support other Indian cities and international jurisdictions through configurable geography, currency, units, language, legal requirements, privacy rules and provider settings.

## 1.3 Product quality objective

The target is a backend that is:

- Domain-owner driven.
- Secure by default.
- Tenant-isolated.
- AI-enabled but not AI-authorized.
- Durable across restarts and infrastructure failures.
- Observable and independently verifiable.
- Recoverable without corrupting financial or business truth.
- Globally configurable.
- Cost-controlled.
- Evidence-driven.
- Capable of governed autonomous business execution.

“World-class”, “autonomous” and “production-ready” are target qualities, not implementation statuses. They may be claimed only when their acceptance evidence exists.

