# 13. Testing and verification architecture

## 13.1 Mandatory test layers

| Layer | Required proof |
|---|---|
| Static/type | Strict compilation, lint and schema consistency |
| Unit | Deterministic behavior of changed code |
| Existing-owner regression | No regression in affected CORE/AI owner |
| API | Route, schema, auth and response behavior |
| Contract | TypeScript/Python/event compatibility |
| Database | Real persistence, transaction and migration behavior |
| Tenancy | Cross-tenant access denial |
| Security | Adversarial authorization and injection tests |
| Event/workflow | Duplicate, replay, timeout and recovery |
| AI | Grounding, retrieval, prompt injection, budget and action safety |
| E2E | Complete real-estate business journeys |
| Performance | Latency, concurrency and load thresholds |
| Operations | Backup, restore, rollback, alert and kill-switch exercises |

No empty test directory counts as test coverage.

## 13.2 Mandatory adversarial tests

Include at minimum:

- Cross-tenant resource ID substitution.
- Forged client tenant ID.
- Privilege escalation.
- Revoked session.
- Expired approval.
- Reused approval proof.
- Modified action payload after approval.
- Duplicate request.
- Duplicate event delivery.
- Out-of-order event.
- Replay after restart.
- Timeout after successful external mutation.
- Provider partial failure.
- Prompt injection inside listing text.
- Prompt injection inside uploaded documents.
- Cross-tenant retrieval contamination.
- Stale inventory response.
- Invalid criteria silently dropped.
- Concurrent financial settlement.
- RLS connection-pool tenant leakage.
- Unauthorized object/document access.
- Kill-switch activation while a workflow is executing.

## 13.3 Financial regression

Financial tests must validate:

- Balanced entries.
- Immutable posting.
- Reversal and adjustment.
- Decimal precision.
- Currency consistency.
- Idempotent commission calculation.
- Concurrent settlement.
- Duplicate payment callback.
- Provider/bank reconciliation.
- Tenant separation.
- Unauthorized posting denial.

## 13.4 AI regression

Tests must prove:

- The AI cannot bypass domain authorization.
- The AI cannot self-approve.
- Retrieval is tenant-scoped.
- Unsupported facts are not invented.
- Tool parameters are validated.
- Tool execution is bounded.
- Cost controls operate before provider invocation.
- Provider fallback preserves policy and authorization.
- Sensitive data is redacted.
- Action evidence is tied to the actual canonical result.

## 13.5 Exact-SHA evidence

Every required CI result must identify:

- Repository.
- Branch.
- Exact tested commit SHA.
- Workflow name.
- Workflow run ID and URL.
- Commands executed.
- Tests discovered.
- Passed, failed, skipped and blocked counts.
- Artifact references.
- Environment classification.
- Remaining blockers.

A successful run on an older SHA is not proof for current HEAD.

Overlapping suites must not be added together and represented as unique test counts.

## 13.6 CI fail-closed conditions

CI must fail when:

- Required checks are missing.
- Required suites unexpectedly discover zero tests.
- Tests are silently skipped.
- Build/type/schema consistency fails.
- Cross-tenant isolation fails.
- Authorization can be bypassed.
- Migrations are unsafe.
- Outbox/inbox or idempotency invariants fail.
- AI quality falls below approved thresholds.
- Critical dependencies or secrets are misconfigured.
- The evidence SHA does not match the tested source.

